          %h2#introduction Introduction
          %p
            In this article we collect some results on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces
            as computed in the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            The account is designed to be parallel to that given in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits+of+normal+spaces"} colimits of normal spaces
          %h2#basic_results Basic results
          #coproduct.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              of a small family of paracompact Hausdorff spaces is a paracompact Hausdorff space.
          %p
            The proof is very easy. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space#ParacompactnessPreservedByDisjointUnion"} here
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subspace"} closed subspace
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of a paracompact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is also a paracompact Hausdorff space.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_\alpha\}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg A \cup U_\alpha
              is the maximal open
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\alpha
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\alpha = V_\alpha \cap A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_\alpha
              cover
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              is a locally finite open refinement of this cover (via paracompactness of
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi V
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V \cap A: V \in \mathcal{V}\}
              is a locally finite open refinement of the family of sets
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_\alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is Hausdorff because Hausdorffness is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hereditary+property"} hereditary property
          #poclosed.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              of a (closed/open) embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              along any continuous map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mi po
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; \stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; B \\
                    \\mathllap{f} \downarrow &amp; po &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{g} \\
                    C &amp; \underset{j}{\hookrightarrow} &amp; D,
                    }
            %p is again a (closed/open) embedding.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For the sake of convenience, we reproduce the proof given
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology#pushout"} here
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Top
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = \hom(1, -): Top \to Set
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has both a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is monic in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              is also a pullback, so that we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley equality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_i \circ f^\ast = g^\ast \exists_j \colon P(C) \to P(B)
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_i \colon P(A) \to P(B)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              map between
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+sets"} power sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast: P(C) \to P(A)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              map).
            %p
              To prove that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is a subspace, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq C
              be any open set. Then there exists open
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subseteq B
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^\ast(V) = f^\ast(U)
              because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a subspace inclusion. If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_U \colon C \to \mathbf{2}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_V \colon B \to \mathbf{2}
              are the maps to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sierpinski+space"} Sierpinski space
              that classify these open sets, then by the universal property of the pushout, there exists a unique continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_W \colon D \to \mathbf{2}
              which extends the pair of maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_U, \chi_V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^{-1}(W) = U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is a subspace inclusion.
            %p
              If moreover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is an open inclusion, then for any open
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq C
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\ast(\exists_j(U)) = U
              (since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is monic) and (by Beck-Chevalley)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\ast(\exists_j(U)) = \exists_i(f^\ast(U))
              is open in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_j(U)
              is open, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is an open inclusion. The same proof, replacing the word “open” with the word “closed” throughout, shows that the pushout of a closed inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is a closed inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %h2#michaels_selection_characterization_of_paracompactness Michael’s selection characterization of paracompactness
          %p
            (See also
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael%27s+theorems"} Michael's theorems
          %p
            It is well-known (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+equivalently+admit+subordinate+partitions+of+unity"} here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a paracompact Hausdorff space if and only if every open cover of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+equivalently+admit+subordinate+partitions+of+unity"} admits a subordinate partition of unity
          %p
            From here on out, all spaces will be assumed to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singletons"} singletons
            are
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+property"} separation property
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is a jointly monic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi R
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mi p
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mi q
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; &amp; R &amp; &amp; \\
                  \&amp; \mathllap{p} \swarrow &amp; &amp; \searrow \mathrlap{q} &amp; \\
                  X &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; Y
                  }
          %p
            and that the relation is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+relation"} entire
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            %em selection
            for such a relation is by definition a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            this means a continuous section. (In the category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            may be equivalently stated as saying that every entire relation admits a selection, a formulation which is sometimes credited to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Sanders+Peirce"} Peirce
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a space, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} X
            denote its topology, considered as a subset of the power set
